. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H1 * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.         * We estimate the causal effect of having a daughter on support for g
> ender equality using a two-stage least squares (2SLS) regression. 
.         *The binary variable has_daughter (1 if the respondent has at least o
> ne daughter) is treated as endogenous and instrumented with the sex of the fi
> rst child (kidsex01), which is assumed to be as good as randomly assigned. 
.         *The outcome variable is gender_equality, a continuous measure of the
>  respondent’s support for gender equality.
.         * To isolate the effect of male respondents we interact the predicted
>  has daughter variable from the first stage with an indicator that is 1 if th
> e respondent of the question is male. 
.         //reg plb0085 d_daughter
.         
.         reg has_daughter kidsex01 log_hghinc bioage male biokids pgpsbil plb0
> 021 sampreg, robust

